# Mobile UI Design System

Full reference: `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md`

## Before changing any UI

Ask: **Can the user do their primary task without scrolling on 390×844?**

**Exception:** Detail pages (Job Details, etc.) — readability first, not ultra-compact.

## Non-negotiables

- **Header**: `UMA SERVICE` + role line (`Jeeva (Technician)`, `Reception`, `Admin`)
- **No redundant headings** on operational pages
- **Job list cards** use `JobListCard` — compact; detail pages use section layout
- **Nav ≤ 5 items**: Home, New Job, Delivery, Pending, Search
- **Call button** wherever customer name/mobile appears
- **Print + Reprint Receipt** on every Job Details page

## Page types

| Type | Style |
|------|-------|
| Operational | Compact, action-first, dense |
| Analytical | Readability first, moderate spacing |
| Detail | Section-based, scannable, spacing OK |

## Role gating

- **Reception**: no collection/revenue reports or totals
- **Admin only**: collection stats, technician revenue, brand reports
- **Technician**: My Jobs first; no service amounts on list cards

## Reception dashboard order

New Job → Search → Ready for Delivery → Today's Stats

## Do not

Redesign functionality — only layout, density, hierarchy, spacing, and mobile usability.
